 body=f'''<h1>{html.escape(c['name'])}<br><small>{t} | SEC-backed equity research companion</small></h1><p class="status"><strong>Partial assignment evidence.</strong> This is a deterministic SEC companion report. No FinRobot LLM agents or FMP calls were run. It does not fulfill the end-to-end report requirement.</p><p>Data cutoff: 2026-10-11. Annual period ended {c.period_end}; annual filing {c.annual_filed}. More recent interim data exist through {c.latest_quarter_end} and are not included in the annual model.</p><div class="grid"><div class="metric">Revenue<strong>${c.revenue_bn:,.3f}bn</strong></div><div class="metric">Revenue growth<strong>{c.revenue_yoy:.1%}</strong></div><div class="metric">CFO less capex proxy<strong>${c.fcf_bn:,.3f}bn</strong></div></div><h2>Investment view and industry comparison</h2><p>{thesis}</p><p>Peer set: {c.peers}. Compare revenue growth, cash generation and margins; current stock returns and peer market multiples are unavailable. Broadcom includes infrastructure software, so this universe is semiconductor-oriented rather than a pure-play homogeneous valuation set.</p><h2>Financial evidence</h2><p>USD financial-statement facts are shown in billions. Shares and EPS retain their native units. Each row links to its filing; the accompanying lineage CSV preserves the exact XBRL tag and accession.</p>{metrics.to_html(index=False,escape=False)}<h2>Revenue forecast</h2><p>Trailing two-year CAGR: {cfg['uncapped_growth']:.1%}; applied growth: {cfg['growth_used']:.1%}, capped at +/-50%. No margin expansion is assumed. Forecast years are strictly after the latest annual observation. This is an extrapolation, not analyst consensus.</p>{revenue.to_html(index=False,float_format=lambda x:f'{x:,.2f}')}<p>Rolling-origin revenue MAPE: baseline {score.baseline_ape:.2%}; CAGR {score.improved_ape:.2%}. The method is not selected for improved pooled accuracy. Acquisition effects, cyclicality and structural breaks are not modeled.</p><h2>Valuation audit</h2><p>Reproduced upstream default DCF: ${c.mechanical_dcf:.2f}/share. This is an arithmetic audit result, not a fair-value recommendation. Inputs: CFO minus capital expenditure proxy, 10% growth for years 1-5, 5% for years 6-10, 10% WACC, 2.5% terminal growth, and synthetic net debt equal to 10% of enterprise value. The cash-flow basis is not validated FCFF; historical period-end shares are used. No market quote, upside or rating is supplied.</p><p>Upstream forecast EBITDA is recomputed as gross profit minus SG&amp;A, omitting R&amp;D. Do not use it as conventional EBITDA without correcting that definition. The scenario sensitivity CSV intentionally preserves this limitation.</p><h2>Risks and remaining work</h2><p>Model risks include fiscal-year alignment, stale annual inputs, share splits, nonuniform XBRL tags, acquisitions, cash-flow classification and unsupported margin assumptions. These are analytical limitations; no company-specific regulatory or supply-chain claim is asserted without source evidence.</p><p>Complete FMP extraction and eight-agent generation, preserve the actual evidence prompt, audit every generated claim, and run frozen-input stability tests before using this as a portfolio-manager report.</p><h2>Sources</h2><p><a href="https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{int({'NVDA':1045810,'AMD':2488,'INTC':50863,'AVGO':1730168,'QCOM':804328}[t]):010d}.json">SEC Company Facts</a> | <a href="{c.source}">Latest annual filing</a> | <a href="https://investors.broadcom.com/static-files/752e631c-b5f3-46af-9d67-bdeb658f5fa2">Broadcom business scope</a></p>'''
